# Winterest project rules for Zed

`AGENTS.md` is the repository source of truth. This file adapts its guidance for Zed; it does not replace it. Before changing code, read `AGENTS.md` and the applicable detailed rules below. `.agents/rules/` remains the canonical source for those detailed rules; open the relevant files because Zed does not load them automatically.

## Always follow

- Use Bun by default. Do not use npm or pnpm unless the user explicitly asks.
- Keep the app compatible with Cloudflare Workers and follow the existing TanStack Start, Tailwind, Radix/shadcn-style, Drizzle, Better Auth, and Cloudflare direction.
- Do not run development servers or database migration/push/pull/studio commands unless the user explicitly asks in the same turn.
- For codebase, architecture, dependency, or feature investigation, consult Graphify first as described in `.agents/rules/graphify.md`. After changing code, follow that file's graph update instruction.
- Keep changes focused. Preserve existing user work and use the repository's verification guidance in `.agents/rules/02-agent-commands-behavior.md` and `.agents/rules/10-code-quality-testing.md`.

## Load detailed rules by task

Read every matching rule file before making changes; read multiple files when a task spans areas.

| When working on... | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Project identity, public brand, UI copy tone, SEO, sitemap, or public-facing content | `.agents/rules/01-identity-branding-copy.md` |
| Package commands, agent behavior, verification, or Definition of Done | `.agents/rules/02-agent-commands-behavior.md` |
| Routes, route files, page responsibilities, or sitemap route registration | `.agents/rules/03-routing-conventions-pages.md` |
| Server/API input validation, HTTP requests, `ofetch`, TanStack Query, forms, or mutations | `.agents/rules/04-server-api-ofetch.md` |
| Cloudflare Workers runtime, D1, Drizzle schema/migrations, R2, or `reset.sql` | `.agents/rules/05-database-cloudflare.md` |
| Better Auth, sessions, password handling, RBAC, secrets, or security | `.agents/rules/06-auth-security-rbac.md` |
| Visual design, design tokens, Tailwind, UI components, animation, accessibility, or 3D | `.agents/rules/07-design-system-ui-3d.md` |
| Feature structure, file/folder naming, components, or module boundaries | `.agents/rules/08-feature-architecture-structure.md` |
| Localized copy, `copy.ts`, static data, or CMS fallback content | `.agents/rules/09-copywriting-data-standards.md` |
| TypeScript/React conventions, state, tests, Git, or code quality | `.agents/rules/10-code-quality-testing.md` |

| Codebase or architecture exploration, graph queries, or graph maintenance | `.agents/rules/graphify.md` |

## Engineering workflow

Use the Matt Pocock engineering skills for planning, ticket breakdown, triage, and implementation: `/to-spec`, `/to-tickets`, `/triage`, `/implement`, or `/implement-spec` as appropriate. Publish change specs and tickets to GitHub Issues. Read `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` and `docs/agents/triage-labels.md` before issue operations, and consult relevant durable domain docs in `docs/features/` and `docs/system/`.

If a task does not fit a category clearly, inspect the relevant rule files before proceeding. Keep the detailed rules in their source files rather than copying them into this always-loaded file.